{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"The allocator test exposed a real translation bug: release optimization had completely removed Rust’s `malloc`/`free` pair and stack-promoted the state, so Rust could never return C’s `-1` allocation failure. I’m fixing the Rust implementation by routing allocation and deallocation through non-inlined helpers, preserving the observable C allocation boundary."}}
